      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.95,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 224,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p4_b13",
      "text": "Closed-form promptwise solutions are insightful, but not yet an RLHF algorithm. The\nfull response simplex is hidden and astronomically large, and the trainable object is the\nLLM parameter vector rather than an explicit probability table. We therefore derive\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        504.95,
        523.35,
        552.69
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        2019,
        2093,
        2210
      ],
      "coord_space": "pdf_points",
      "font_size": 11.84,
      "font_name": "LMRoman12-Regular",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 257,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p4_b14",
      "text": "policy-gradient surrogates for DRRO, show that the robust correction appears as a simple\nreward bonus, and replace the exact maximum by a smooth maximum estimated from\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        558.73,
        523.36,
        588.54
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
